From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: thisiscamk <100883750+thisiscamk@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 21:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: s5l8960x: Wake on the D2089 source event

A live unplug/replug cycle on the iPad Air (Cellular) latched D2089 event
0 at the replug edge.  This is also the event identified as the D2089 plug
event from iOS 12 when support for this PMIC was added.

Give that event to the charger after its line and ADC interrupts.  The
charger can then arm the real PMIC event as a wake source instead of
relying on polling while the system is asleep.  Every A7 iPad has the
same D2089 and charger node, so this goes in the iPad Air and iPad mini
2/3 files they share.

Tested on an iPad Air (Cellular, J72).

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: thisiscamk <100883750+thisiscamk@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s5l8960x-air1.dtsi  | 7 ++++---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s5l8960x-mini2.dtsi | 7 ++++---
 2 files changed, 8 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s5l8960x-air1.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s5l8960x-air1.dtsi
index 4a807b073..9c95a1c6c 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s5l8960x-air1.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s5l8960x-air1.dtsi
@@ -199,11 +199,12 @@ tristar_charger: charger@60 {
 		reg-names = "status", "control", "adc";
 		interrupt-parent = <&pmu_events>;
 		/*
-		 * The PMU line and ADC done. No source events, as on the iPad
-		 * Air 2: the charger's 100 ms poll of 0x60 sees plug and unplug.
+		 * The PMU line, ADC done and the D2089's plug event (event 0),
+		 * which wakes the system when the source changes during sleep.
 		 */
 		interrupts = <112 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>,
-			     <89 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>;
+			     <89 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>,
+			     <0 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>;
 		apple,tristar = <&tristar>;
 		input-current-limit-microamp = <1500000>;
 
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s5l8960x-mini2.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s5l8960x-mini2.dtsi
index 460683c73..2df5c1053 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s5l8960x-mini2.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s5l8960x-mini2.dtsi
@@ -121,11 +121,12 @@ tristar_charger: charger@60 {
 		reg-names = "status", "control", "adc";
 		interrupt-parent = <&pmu_events>;
 		/*
-		 * The PMU line and ADC done. No source events, as on the iPad
-		 * Air 2: the charger's 100 ms poll of 0x60 sees plug and unplug.
+		 * The PMU line, ADC done and the D2089's plug event (event 0),
+		 * which wakes the system when the source changes during sleep.
 		 */
 		interrupts = <112 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>,
-			     <89 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>;
+			     <89 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>,
+			     <0 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>;
 		apple,tristar = <&tristar>;
 		input-current-limit-microamp = <1500000>;
 
